{"agent_id":"pp3g-2jFS-adversarially-review-the-wave-based-execution-plan","agent_seq":2,"timestamp":"2026-08-01T00:42:37.884748794Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"55c73bbe-48d1-4e77-810f-0247f3ad4bda","comment_uuid":"179b486c-3d5e-4d25-96be-c91737d97fdd","author":"pp3g-2jFS-adversarially-review-the-wave-based-execution-plan","content":"## REVIEW (1/3): Verdict + Wave ordering — CHANGES REQUESTED\n\nIndependent adversarial review of the PLAN comment (2026-08-01 00:34). I read all 10 sub-issues #109-#118, verified claims against the live repo and CLI, and reproduced the #109 defect in this very session. The plan is directionally sound and honestly sequenced, but it has 3 blocking gaps and several hidden dependencies.\n\n### Q1: Is the wave ordering correct?\n\nVERDICT: Mostly correct (0→1→2→3 matches the critical path), but with hidden dependencies and one security-relevant omission.\n\n1. MUST FIX — #113 (bulk-close) has a hidden dependency on #112 (locks). 8 of the stale test issues (#33, #34, #35, #64, #66, #71, #92, #93) are currently locked by OL2r (crosslink locks list). If close refuses on locked issues, #113 stalls. Sequence #112 before #113, or verify close-on-locked behavior first.\n\n2. MUST FIX — #113's selection needs explicit exclusions. Do NOT bulk-close #73/#74 (they are completed but their findings/ deliverables are unmerged — #114 must merge them first, else the tracker loses the only copies of that work), and exclude #106-#108 (the active test cycle) plus #109-#118 (this plan) and #14-#21/#22-#27 (real work). close-all has no status filter in its help; verify it only touches open issues and pass a precise filter.\n\n3. MUST FIX — #109 has an unresolved fork (align enforcement vs deny bash) that determines what Wave 2's docs must say. #114/#115/#116/#117 all touch KICKOFF.md and/or agent templates; #116 and #109 both touch .opencode/plugins/crosslink-guard.ts. Decide the #109 direction BEFORE Wave 2 or Wave 2 will need rework. If #109 picks deny-bash, KICKOFF.md's 'Always allowed' section and 'Reviewing Previous Phase Output' (git fetch/diff/show) must be rewritten — a much bigger doc change than #116 currently scopes.\n\n4. SHOULD CONSIDER — Wave ordering is not encoded in the tracker: #109-#118 ALL appear in 'crosslink issue ready' today. Add blocked_by edges so #118 cannot be launched before #109/#111/#117; otherwise a future agent following 'ready' can start Wave 3 early (the exact premature-PASS risk the plan exists to prevent).\n\n5. SHOULD CONSIDER — #112 enabling auto_steal_stale_locks=true is risky as scoped. My own lock on #78 (claimed minutes ago) already displays [STALE] in 'crosslink locks list', and heartbeat hooks are not deployed (workflow diff: all 6 .claude/hooks/*.py missing), so staleness detection cannot distinguish an active agent from an abandoned one. Auto-steal could steal an active agent's lock mid-run — including during Wave 3. Verify the staleness heuristic against active sessions before enabling auto_steal.\n\n6. NIT — Priorities: #109/#110/#111/#112/#118 say 'High.' in their descriptions but are all priority=medium. If the tracker is the triage source (the premise of #113), priorities should match reality.","created_at":"2026-08-01T00:42:37.878927026Z","kind":"observation","signed_by":"SHA256:Gi1NETEhXFIBL4GtTZRThUsMrSDXxKbs3BxJwTdcMtc","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgv8dUcKPG4MDQ4aGd595Nw1cDFZDGHt3ijkENij13zrwAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABABt5cDNY6LF3n7LbbBQtsnsNO0IfoENLN0cWS3jRa4/BNIwd1b804/5M0NoQsKVsak9e1lAedc8tYPgvasOs+Dg=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:Gi1NETEhXFIBL4GtTZRThUsMrSDXxKbs3BxJwTdcMtc","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgv8dUcKPG4MDQ4aGd595Nw1cDFZDGHt3ijkENij13zrwAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQGexRGCfVBwxPm4EPi8Ci3To76sfVRiUPTJdU0UUhviB+iMH1qwuPtSw/kvbT1Bopd/dhwehGbmVr62WRaEvdAA="}
